Both are ideally identical.
Remember that the DXS -> PCM mapping is introduced just because of
most of user's expectation: they need a PCM control.
That is, DXS->PCM mapping is the "normal" behavior from both
viewpoints.  No need to inform users the "normal" behavior.

On the contrary, user would think that they hit a bug if they see a
warning message.

I understand that you're tempted to add this as a coder, though.

> Which didn't solve anything, because every user expect different thing :-)

